  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2016-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The expression is equivalent to \\[2a^{-2}+\\frac{a^{-2}}{2} = 2.5 (a^{-1})^2.\\] Then \\(a^{-1} \\) is equal to \\(\\dfrac{1}{\\frac 12} = 2,\\) so our expression is equal to \\(2.5\\cdot 2^2 = 10.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D .",
      "hints": [
        "Substitute \\(a=\\frac{1}{2}\\) after combining powers of \\(a\\)",
        "Dividing by \\(a\\) turns \\(a^{-1}\\) into \\(a^{-2}\\)"
      ],
